                <pb facs="0831" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/595: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-04T13:00:00+09:00">March 4, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 4—1 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Department’s 28, March 3, 5 p.m. The Embassy is now compiling a despatch
                    containing all available official announcements, official radio broadcasts,
                    leaflets, et cetera, which will be transmitted in the pouch due Washington March
                        21.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d757-f1"/> It is improbable, however, that all the
                    official details desired by the Department will be available for some time to
                    come owing to continued censorship and the fact that even the officials of the
                    Foreign Office are not yet certain of all the details. The whole subject will be
                    fully covered in due course.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
